# pstack model configuration. One line per role. Keep every line. A missing line falls back to a fast model.
# grok-4.7 with fast off. No slug ends in `-fast`. No role defaults to xhigh.
# Default effort is medium (`grok-4.7-medium`).
# High (`grok-4.7-high`) is for hard debugging, migrations, `bug-fix`, `hardest tasks`, `arena runners`, `arena cross-judge pool`, and `architect runners`.
# xhigh only when the person launching the agent asks for it for a big multi-part plan and states why. Never a file default. Never for audit or design work.
# Never `auto`, `default`, or `inherit-parent`. Those omit the model and the helper falls back to a fast model.
# Never composer. Never any slug ending in `-fast`, including `grok-4.7-xhigh-fast` and `composer-2.5-fast`.
# Do not turn fast on, including when a job is urgent or a skill says to pick a speed.
# If you cannot set the line's slug, do that work yourself. Do not substitute a fast model.
# budget: mixed (medium default, high for bug-fix, hardest tasks, arena, and architect), fast off. No xhigh default.
feature, refactoring: grok-4.7-medium
bug-fix: grok-4.7-high
perf-issue: grok-4.7-medium
hillclimb: grok-4.7-medium
judgment and prose: grok-4.7-medium
hardest tasks: grok-4.7-high
